# Copy to .env.local and fill in from Supabase > Project Settings > API.
#
# Absent, the app runs exactly as it did before accounts existed: no Supabase
# client is constructed and the Account item is hidden. That is the tested
# fallback, not a broken state.
#
# The key is the publishable (formerly anon) one, which is meant to be public
# and ships in the browser bundle. Row Level Security is what protects the data.
# The secret / service_role key must never appear here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Where crashes are reported, from Sentry > Settings > Projects > Client Keys.
#
# Absent, the app still catches its own crashes and still offers to email them.
# Nothing is imported and nothing leaves the browser. That is how the tests run
# and how every build ran before 2026-08-09.
#
# A DSN is an ingest address, not a password. It only lets the holder send
# events in, so it is meant to ship in the browser bundle. It lives in an
# environment variable so it can be changed or removed without a code change.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Server only
#
# No VITE_ prefix, on purpose. Vite only puts VITE_ variables in the bundle, and
# the one below is a password: anything holding it can send mail as the domain.
# It belongs in Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables, not in a file that
# ships. This copy is only here so `vercel dev` can run the function locally.
#
# From Resend > API Keys. Absent, api/feedback.ts answers 503 and Suggest a
# Feature says sending is not set up. That is the tested fallback, and the app
# is otherwise unaffected.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Both optional. Where feedback lands defaults to FEEDBACK_EMAIL in
# src/lib/appInfo.ts, which is the address the app already shows people, so
# there is only ever one to change. The from address has to sit on a domain
# verified in Resend.
FEEDBACK_TO=
FEEDBACK_FROM=
